       <item>
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_descstats_help">
         <property name="minimumSize">
          <size>
           <width>0</width>
           <height>30</height>
          </size>
         </property>
         <property name="maximumSize">
          <size>
           <width>16777215</width>
           <height>30</height>
          </size>
         </property>
         <property name="toolTip">
          <string>Calculate runs all the statistics in the report. 
Text statistics (corpus summary, frequency table, hapax, breakdown by the partition variable) and, when a partition variable is selected, the chi-square specificities (green = over-represented, red = under-represented). 
Definitions:
Segments = the analysed text units (coded texts of the selected codes, or whole documents)
Occurrences = total number of words
Forms = distinct word forms after normalisation
Active forms = forms occurring at least the minimum frequency (rarer forms are supplementary)
Hapax = forms occurring only once.</string>
         </property>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Text statistics report (summary, frequency table, hapax, partition variable breakdown). Partition variable: chi-square specificities shown (green = over-represented, red = under-represented).</string>
         </property>
         <property name="wordWrap">
          <bool>true</bool>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
